// EXPECT: [E100]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 8, Col 9: a \x escape takes exactly two hex digits
// A `\x` escape takes exactly two hex digits, in a string as in a character literal (spec 05). The
// digit helper printed "invalid hex digit in char literal" to STDOUT and returned 0, so `'\xZ1'`
// compiled to 1; a string took whatever digits it found, so `"\x4"` was one byte and `"\xZZ"` a
// NUL and "ZZ", silently. Found by the Debugger agent, whose probe's stdout the message corrupted.
func main() i32 {
    c = '\xZ1'
    return c as i32
}
